      },
      "question": {
        ":question/id": "e15ff6ee-c2f1-56bf-9468-67d246f13bf8",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "If $f(x)=\\frac{x}{\\sin x},$ find ${f}^{\\prime}(x).$\n\n${f}^{\\prime}(x)=$\n{{field-1}}",
        ":question/worked-solution": "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=x$ and $v(x)=\\sin x.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\\prime}(x)&=\\frac{u^{\\prime}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot v^{\\prime}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{(x)^{\\prime}\\cdot (\\sin{\\left(x \\right)})-(x)\\cdot (\\sin{\\left(x \\right)})^{\\prime}}{(\\sin{\\left(x \\right)})^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{1\\cdot \\sin x-x\\cdot \\cos x}{\\sin ^{2}x}\\\\ &=\\frac{\\sin x-xcosx}{\\sin ^{2}x}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "09f8a235-306c-5a3f-8d31-69f8b2cccc9f",
            ":answer-field/key": "field-1",
            ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/blank",
